Done. Task 2 is implemented, verified, and committed as 5adc49a5.

## What I built

Step 1 — a pure per-session bucketing core in scripts/extract_trajectory.py:

• `collect_task_commit_times() — one git log --format=%H%x09%ct%x09%s pass keeping (sha, epoch, subject) triples matching TASK_COMMIT_RE`, plus the epoch of the oldest commit reachable in the clone.
• `load_claim_sessions() — the window's sessions with their claims, newest-first. load_outcomes now delegates to a shared iter_session_outcomes`, so there is one statement of which sessions are in the window.
• `classify_session_claims(sessions, commits, oldest_commit_epoch) — pure, five states, none folded: CORROBORATED, CLAIM_NO_COMMITS, NO_CLAIM, COULD_NOT_CHECK, CLAIM_OPEN_WINDOW`.
• `PRODUCTIVITY_IDLE / classify_productivity` are untouched.

Step 2 — rendered beside each claim: render_outcomes(outcomes, session_claims) keeps its claim rows byte-identical and appends one ⚠ <session dir>: claimed success, 0 task commits in this session's window line per flagged session, plus the count line naming its own population (N of M closed, claiming session(s)), with unresolvable windows on a separate line.

## Two things I found that the plan did not anticipate

1. **The open-window rule and the "print a zero" rule pull apart.** New content cannot be added and change nothing. The only coherent reading is that the *claim row block* is byte-identical — I pinned that three ways with `assert_eq!` on the whole render, including asserting the all-corroborated render carries no `⚠` anywhere. I stated this explicitly in ARCHITECTURE.md rather than smoothing it.
2. **The shallow clone is a false-alarm generator.** A recent session's task commits sit *outside* the 50-commit checkout while the only in-window commits are `bump counter` bookkeeping — so the clone boundary is a refusal (COULD_NOT_CHECK), not an accusation. That is why the live reading is 6 ... could NOT be checked instead of a page of false positives.

