• `python3 scripts/extract_trajectory.py --test — **ALL PASSED**; bash tests/harness_logic.sh OK; python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts` — 38 tests OK.
• **Live run on this repo: `0 of 3 closed, claiming session(s): claimed success, no task commits` + `6 further claiming session(s) could NOT be checked (window unresolved)`. The null is the result** — zero flagged sessions, with the counts and the population named.
• **Positive control, run serially as one atomic mutate→run→restore:** neutering the classifier returned `CORROBORATED` unconditionally reddening 5 tests, the discriminating one by name (`discriminating: the SIBLING ON THE SAME DAY with zero commits is FLAGGED`); restore returned ALL PASSED. 0 markers left in the tree.
• The discriminating row is asserted in both directions: the sibling is flagged and classify_productivity still reads that same day as PRODUCTIVITY_OK — proof the day-level check cannot see it.
